Listtree.mcc/Listtree.mcc

    NAME
        Listtree.mcc -- Display a tree through an NListtree adapter.

    SUPERCLASS
        List.mui

    INPUTS
        Create Listtree.mcc with the supported construction attributes below.
        The pinned class configuration declares version 0.11.

    FUNCTION
        This List subclass uses an internal NListtree object. Its public nodes
        are MUIS_Listtree_TreeNode proxies, not MUI_NListtree_TreeNode
        pointers. Use nodes returned by Insert, GetEntry, FindName or TestPos
        with the same object. Do not copy, free or fabricate them. Removal and
        disposal invalidate them.
        tn_Name is borrowed from the backend; tn_User is application data or
        the construct-hook result. tn_Private1 and tn_Private2 are private.
        TNF_LIST marks a branch and TNF_OPEN its expanded state. Flags are
        synchronized only at selected adapter calls and hooks; they are not a
        continuously updated state view.
        Active has an inconsistent representation: the getter returns an
        internal pointer, whereas setter/method inputs use proxies and Active
        notifications translate to proxies. Obtain the active proxy with
        GetEntry using Position_Active.
        Only the documented construction subset is forwarded. ContextMenu goes
        to List; Frame, List_Title, List_DragSortable and List_MinLineHeight
        also have explicit child forwarding. This is not a complete Listtree
        compatibility implementation. SetDropMark is a stub. List_First is
        ignored on set and does not provide working notifications here.
        Keep hook structures, hook data and borrowed payloads valid until
        their final use, including disposal. Use the owning application
        context. Hooks are synchronous; avoid reentrant mutation that
        invalidates nodes being processed.
        Failure handling is incomplete for child/pool/proxy/image allocation.
        Image text conversion requires valid writable strings and matching
        handles. No general low-memory recovery or arbitrary-input validation
        guarantee is provided.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_Active

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_Active -- Set or read the active tree node.

    INPUTS
        Set/get; a live same-object proxy on set. Not initialized by this
        constructor.

    FUNCTION
        Set dereferences the supplied proxy without NULL/sentinel handling.
        Get returns the raw internal NListtree node, not the public proxy.
        Forwarded Active notifications carry the proxy or zero. Do not feed
        the getter result back into the setter.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_Quiet

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_Quiet -- Set or read quiet mode.

    INPUTS
        Set/get; BOOL. Not initialized by this constructor.

    FUNCTION
        Forward to NListtree_Quiet and bridge its notifications. Use it to
        batch display changes; this adapter does not promise suppression of
        all notifications or balanced nesting. NoNotify on the outer set is
        not propagated into separate child set calls.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_DoubleClick

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_DoubleClick -- Read the double-click state.

    INPUTS
        Get/notification; the header labels this set/get BOOL.

    FUNCTION
        Read the backend DoubleClick value and bridge its notifications
        unchanged. The local setter does not forward this attribute to
        NListtree; do not use it to configure backend double-click behavior.
        Construction does not process it.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_ConstructHook

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_ConstructHook -- Provide the node construction hook at initialization.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; struct Hook * or NULL.

    FUNCTION
        Borrow the hook. CallHookPkt receives the instance pool as object and
        incoming User as message. Store the returned payload in proxy tn_User.
        NULL hook retains incoming User. A NULL hook result is not treated as
        an insertion rejection. The adapter allocates the proxy separately.
        Pair payload ownership with DestructHook.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_DestructHook

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_DestructHook -- Provide the node destruction hook at initialization.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; struct Hook * or NULL.

    FUNCTION
        Borrow the hook and call it with pool as object and proxy tn_User as
        message before releasing each proxy. Without a hook, the adapter does
        not free application payloads. The pool remains live during child
        disposal. Do not free the proxy itself in the hook.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_DisplayHook

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_DisplayHook -- Provide the display hook at initialization.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; struct Hook * or NULL.

    FUNCTION
        CallHookPkt receives the column-string array as object and public
        proxy as message, or NULL for a title row. Return the display result.
        Provide valid column strings and the terminating NULL pointer expected
        by the adapter. It may rewrite image escape text in place, so such
        strings must be writable and contain valid matching CreateImage
        handles. It handles only the first image escape per column and does
        not guarantee every address width.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_SortHook

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_SortHook -- Provide the sort hook at initialization.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; struct Hook * or NULL.

    FUNCTION
        Invoke the borrowed hook with first proxy as object and second proxy
        as message after synchronizing flags. Return the comparison result to
        the backend. Without this hook, NListtree retains its own comparison
        behavior. Do not invalidate nodes during comparison.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_Title

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_Title -- Select title display at initialization.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; BOOL.

    FUNCTION
        Translate to NListtree_Title during child construction. No local
        set/get forwarding is implemented. The backend determines layout and
        default.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_Format

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_Format -- Specify the column format at initialization.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; readable STRPTR.

    FUNCTION
        Translate the column-format string to NListtree_Format during
        construction. No local setter/getter or independent storage contract
        is added; use the backend format syntax and lifetime rules.
Listtree.mcc/MUIA_Listtree_DragDropSort

    NAME
        MUIA_Listtree_DragDropSort -- Select drag-and-drop sorting at initialization.

    INPUTS
        Initialize only; BOOL.

    FUNCTION
        Translate to NListtree_DragDropSort during construction. It controls
        backend sorting by drag and drop; it does not implement SetDropMark.
        No local set/get forwarding.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_Insert

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_Insert -- Insert a node.

    INPUTS
        Name, User, ListNode, PrevNode, Flags. Use live proxies from this
        object, or only the named selectors for this method. Other integer
        values are not validated.

    FUNCTION
        ListNode accepts Root (0), Active (-2), or a proxy. PrevNode accepts
        Head (0), Tail (-1), Active (-2), Sorted (-4), or a proxy to insert
        after. The backend defaults to copying names; the adapter installs no
        alternative name-ownership setting.
        TNF_LIST creates a branch; TNF_OPEN marks it open. Flags_Active
        activates the new node and can open its parents. The header also
        defines Flags_NextNode, but the pinned backend Insert does not test
        that bit. Do not assume insertion-before behavior from it.
        The constructor hook receives User. The backend node is created before
        the adapter finishes the proxy name, flags and back-reference. Hooks
        or notifications during insertion must not assume that proxy
        initialization has finished.

    RESULT
        Borrowed new proxy or NULL on a reported failure. Allocation failures
        are not uniformly handled; this is not an atomic-operation guarantee.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_GetEntry

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_GetEntry -- Find a node by position.

    INPUTS
        Node, Position, Flags. Use live proxies from this object, or only the
        named selectors for this method. Other integer values are not
        validated.

    FUNCTION
        Node accepts Root (0), Active (-2), or a proxy. Position accepts Head
        (0), Tail (-1), Active (-2), Next (-3), Previous (-4), Parent (-5), or
        a nonnegative traversal index. Next/Previous refer to siblings of
        Node; Parent asks for its parent.
        Flags_Visible and Flags_SameLevel are forwarded for indexed traversal.
        Direct special-position cases do not apply those filters. The hidden
        root has no public proxy, so a top-level parent is returned as NULL.
        Flags on a found proxy are synchronized.

    RESULT
        Borrowed proxy or NULL.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_FindName

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_FindName -- Find a named node.

    INPUTS
        ListNode, Name, Flags. Use live proxies from this object, or only the
        named selectors for this method. Other integer values are not
        validated.

    FUNCTION
        ListNode accepts Root (0), Active (-2), or a proxy. Supply a readable
        name. Delegate the name comparison and depth-first search to
        NListtree. Flags_Visible restricts candidates to visible nodes;
        Flags_SameLevel prevents descent. The adapter supplies no own
        name-comparison hook and does not synchronize returned proxy flags.

    RESULT
        Borrowed proxy or NULL.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_GetNr

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_GetNr -- Get a position or count.

    INPUTS
        TreeNode, Flags. Supply a real proxy or Active (-2); NULL is not a
        root selector in this adapter.

    FUNCTION
        With no count flags, return the backend tree position, or -1 when not
        found. Flags_ListEmpty returns whether a branch is empty; a leaf gives
        zero. Flags_CountList returns entries in the branch, CountLevel
        entries in its parent list, and CountAll all entries.
        The backend tests ListEmpty, CountList, applicable CountLevel, then
        CountAll in that order; flags are not independent output requests.
        Active requires an existing active node on dereferencing paths.

    RESULT
        Backend position, count or boolean; zero has different meanings
        according to Flags.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_Remove

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_Remove -- Remove nodes.

    INPUTS
        ListNode, TreeNode, Flags. Use live proxies from this object, or only
        the named selectors for this method. Other integer values are not
        validated.

    FUNCTION
        ListNode accepts Root (0), Active (-2), or a proxy. TreeNode accepts
        Head (0), Tail (-1), Active (-2), All (-3), or a proxy. Forward flags
        unchanged; Visible and Nr flags are explicitly unsupported in the
        Listtree header.
        Removing nodes releases their proxies and runs the optional payload
        destructor. Removed branch contents are also invalidated. Do not
        retain or reuse removed-node pointers.

    RESULT
        The pinned backend returns zero; this is not a success or
        removed-count report.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_Rename

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_Rename -- Change node data.

    INPUTS
        TreeNode, NewName, Flags. Supply a proxy or Active (-2).

    FUNCTION
        Without Flags_User, rename the backend node and update the returned
        proxy name. Supply a readable NUL-terminated NewName. Flags_NoRefresh
        suppresses the backend redraw.
        Flags_User is defined but does not preserve a usable proxy here:
        backend destruction frees the old proxy, construction allocates a
        replacement, and this wrapper updates only tn_Name, not its backend
        reference or flags. Existing aliases become invalid. This path is not
        a supported replacement for assigning application payload through a
        stable node.

    RESULT
        Returned proxy or NULL; return alone does not establish a valid proxy
        after Flags_User.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_Open

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_Open -- Open branches.

    INPUTS
        ListNode, TreeNode, Flags. Use live proxies from this object, or only
        the named selectors for this method. Other integer values are not
        validated.

    FUNCTION
        ListNode accepts Root (0), Parent (-1), Active (-2), or a proxy.
        TreeNode accepts Head (0), Tail (-1), Active (-2), All (-3), or a
        proxy. Parent starts at the root and also opens ancestors of the
        target. All requests recursive expansion. Flags pass unchanged;
        Visible and Nr flags are unsupported in the header. Cached public
        tn_Flags are not refreshed by this wrapper.

    RESULT
        Zero from the pinned backend, not a success report.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_Close

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_Close -- Close branches.

    INPUTS
        ListNode, TreeNode, Flags. Use live proxies from this object, or only
        the named selectors for this method. Other integer values are not
        validated.

    FUNCTION
        ListNode accepts Root (0), Parent (-1), Active (-2), or a proxy.
        TreeNode accepts Head (0), Tail (-1), Active (-2), All (-3), or a
        proxy. Parent resolves the parent of the active list and requires
        valid active-list state. All requests recursive collapse. Flags pass
        unchanged; Visible and Nr flags are unsupported in the header. Cached
        public tn_Flags are not refreshed by this wrapper.

    RESULT
        Zero from the pinned backend, not a success report.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_TestPos

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_TestPos -- Identify the node at a position.

    INPUTS
        X, Y, Result. Result must point to writable
        MUIS_Listtree_TestPos_Result storage.

    FUNCTION
        Forward coordinates to backend hit testing. Translate the node to its
        public proxy and copy placement into tpr_Flags, plus list entry and
        list flags. Placement values are None (0), Above (1), Below (2), Onto
        (3); Sorted (4) is defined but not produced by the reviewed backend
        path.
        A hit synchronizes node flags. No hit sets node NULL, entry -1 and
        flags zero through the backend result. The result node is borrowed; it
        does not keep the node alive.

    RESULT
        TRUE for a found node, otherwise FALSE. This differs from the backend
        method return value, which is ignored.
Listtree.mcc/MUIM_Listtree_SetDropMark

    NAME
        MUIM_Listtree_SetDropMark -- Report an unsupported operation.

    INPUTS
        Entry, Values. The header defines Values_None (0).

    FUNCTION
        The adapter only prints a diagnostic. It does not create, move or
        clear a drop mark.

    RESULT
        Always FALSE.

